{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed externally illuminated free standing sign, by reason of its siting and scale, would result in an obtrusive and incongruous appearance, which would\r\nfail to respect the character of the locality and the street scene. It would\r\ntherefore fail to preserve public visual amenity, contrary to the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D8 of The London Plan (2021), and Policies DM1 and DM5 of the Development\r\nManagement Policies Local plan (2013) .&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\nexternally illuminated free-standing advertisement sign, by reason of its\r\nsiting, proximity to the front bay window of the adjoining residential property\r\nat No. 97 Marsh Lane, and its external illumination, would result in\r\nunacceptable harm to the residential amenity of neighbouring occupiers through\r\nincreased light spill and visual intrusion. The proposal is therefore contrary\r\nto the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D8 of the London Plan\r\n(2021), and Policies DM1 and DM5 of the Development Management Policies Local\r\nplan (2013).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
